# basePath ResearchIntroCh2

::IntroSelectTrace
@trigger    OnSetupComplete
$if MinigameHasValidSolution()
    {@PAL}  You've already researched everything you need to!
$else
    $set temp:needsToOpenWikiFirstTime = true
    $call   ShowPrimaryPALButton("OpenProperties")
    {@PAL}  This contract specifies that we need to research a semiconductor. I recommend you open up the ships database to learn properties a semiconductor component has.
$endif


::OnWikiClosed
@trigger    OnWikiClosed
@when       !MinigameHasValidSolution(), temp:needsToOpenWikiFirstTime
$set temp:needsToOpenWikiFirstTime = false
{@PAL}      Interesting. Semiconductors allow current to pass, and current increases when heat is applied. \n\nI recommend you add a material to the voltage chamber to begin testing.


::OnPlaceIntoSlot
@trigger    OnSlotFilled
@when       slotType == "primary", !MinigameHasValidSolution()
{@PAL}      Now apply voltage to to test the sample’s electrical properties


::OnVoltageIncreased
@trigger    OnVoltageIncreased
@when       !MinigameHasValidSolution()
$call   ShowPrimaryPALButton("OpenObservations")
{@PAL}      It looks like this sample allows voltage to pass. Open your database to the Observations tab and click on the observation to record it.


::OnLastWikiClosed
@trigger    OnWikiClosed
@when       MinigameHasValidSolution()
$call       ReleaseAllHighlights()
$call       HighlightElement(return-button)
{@PAL}      You've completed all research tasks. Press the back button to return to the ship.